cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Visible States: statistical reporting across countries, policy sectors, and time"
message: "If you use these scores or this code, please cite the work below."
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Sanchez
    given-names: Sevastian
    affiliation: "Columbia University"
    email: ss7257@columbia.edu
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0007-2792-8115"
abstract: >-
  The first transparency measure covering the SDG era: latent reporting
  behaviour across 524 statistical series and 197 countries, 2015-2023, with
  uncertainty quantified for every country-year. Visible States Index
  (VSI) gives each country-year a single score, estimated by item response
  theory on the UN Global SDG Indicators Database. Sector-level scores and
  per-series item parameters accompany it.
keywords:
  - transparency
  - missing data
  - Sustainable Development Goals
  - item response theory
  - official statistics
  - data availability
  - democratic backsliding
